people approach housing services when  they're facing problems with where they  live these include being unable to pay  their rental mortgage being told to  leave by parents or fleeing violence  also where properties are unsuitable for  them due to disrepair such as severe  damp or having no heating as well as  being unable to use a bathroom  to solve these problems we try to help  people in their homes we offer advice  about housing rights links to specialist  services and support help with  adaptations such as level access showers  or stair lifts and financial assistance  to repair and improve properties  if it is not possible to remain at home  we also help people to move we work to  link people with private landlords to  find a new place to rent and help people  applying for affordable social housing  in order to do this we try to maximize  the accommodation available  we work with housing associations to  build new housing where people want to  live as well as the owners of empty  properties to bring them back into use
 

